्य सः","one for whom that alone is the goal"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":8,"end":8,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["धर्मार्थः धर्म-कामः","one who desires righteousness"],["उत्तम-श्लोकोपाधिं विष्णुम्","Viṣṇu, the object of praise in excellent verses"],["तन्तुं तन्वन्","extending the line"],["सन्तान-वृद्धिम् अन्विच्छन्","seeking the increase of offspring"],["रक्षा बाधा-निवृत्तिः","protection means removal of obstacles"],["पुण्य-जनान् यक्षान्","the puṇya-janas, the Yakṣas"],["ओजः बलम्","ojas means strength"],["मरुद्-गणान् देवान्","the gods called the Maruts"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":9,"end":9,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["राज्यं राजत्वम्","kingdom means kingship"],["मनून् देवान् मन्वन्तर-पालान्","the Manus, divine rulers of the manvantaras"],["राज्ञः कर्म राज्यं","a king's duty is governance"],["विश्वान् देवान्","the Viśve-devas"],["अभिचरन्","one performing an abhichāra rite"],["शत्रु-मरणम् इच्छन्","desiring the death of an enemy"],["निरृतिं राक्षसम्","Nirṛti, the Rākṣasa deity"],["काम-कामः भोगेच्छुः","one who desires pleasure is desirous of objects"],["अकामः वैराग्य-कामः","one without material desire seeks detachment"],["पुरुषं परं ईश्वरम्","the Supreme Person, the Lord"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":10,"end":10,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["अकामः","one without material desire"],["एकान्त-भक्तः","an exclusive devotee"],["उक्तानुक्त-सर्व-कामः वा","or one with every desire, stated or unstated"],["पुरुषं पूर्णम्","the complete Supreme Person"],["निरुपाधिम्","free of limiting adjuncts"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":11,"end":11,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["नाना-देवता-यजनस्य","of worshiping various deities"],["संयोग-पृथक्त्वेन","through combination and distinctness"],["भक्ति-योग-फलत्वम्","its becoming a result of bhakti-yoga"],["इन्द्रादीन् अपि यजताम्","even for those worshiping Indra and the others"],["भगवत्य् अचलो भावो भक्तिः","steadfast feeling for Bhagavān, devotion"],["एतावान् एव निःश्रेयसस्य उदयः","this alone is the arising of the highest good"],["परम-पुरुषार्थस्य लाभः","the attainment of the supreme human goal"],["अन्यत् तु सर्वं तुच्छम्","everything else is insignificant"],["तत्-तद्-यजनेन भागवतानां सङ्गतः","through worship of each deity, association with devotees"],["भगवत्य् अचलो भावो भक्तिर् भवति","steadfast devotion to Bhagavān arises"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":12,"end":12,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["ज्ञानं भवति","knowledge arises"],["प्रतिनिवृत्तम् उपरतम्","withdrawn, having subsided"],["गुणोर्मीणां रागादीनाम्","from the waves of the qualities, beginning with passion"],["चक्रं समूहः","a cycle, a collection"],["आत्म-प्रसादः","serenity of the self"],["मनः-प्रसाद-हेतुः","the cause of serenity of mind"],["गुणेषु विषयेषु असङ्गः वैराग्यम्","detachment from the qualities, the sense objects"],["कैवल्यम् इति संमतः पन्थाः","the path known as liberation"],["भक्ति-योगः","bhakti-yoga"],["श्रवण-सुखेन निर्वृतः","satisfied by the happiness of hearing"],["तासु हरि-कथासु रतिम्","delight in those narrations of Hari"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":13,"end":13,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["अभिव्याहृतम् उक्तम्","what has been spoken"],["ऋषिम् पर-ब्रह्म-दर्शिनम्","the sage who has seen the Supreme Brahman"],["कविम् शब्द-ब्रह्म-निष्णातम्","the poet deeply versed in the Veda"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":14,"end":14,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["श्रवणेच्छायां हेतुः","the reason for the desire to hear"],["हरि-कथा एव उदर्कः","the narrations of Hari alone are the future fruit"],["उत्तर-फलं यासु","those in which the later result is found"],["सतां भागवतानाम्","of the devotees"],["सदसि सभायाम्","in the assembly"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":15,"end":15,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["एतत् प्रपञ्चयति","he elaborates this"],["कृष्ण-पूजादि-रूपाम्","in the form of worship of Kṛṣṇa and the like"],["क्रीडाम्","play"],["यः स्वीकृतवान्","who accepted"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":16,"end":16,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["उरुगायस्य गुणैः","by the qualities of the greatly praised Lord"],["उदाराः महत्यः कथाः","noble, great narrations"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":17,"end":17,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["क्षीयमाणम् आयुः","life that is passing away"],["हरि-कथया सफलं कुर्व्","make it fruitful through narrations of Hari"],["असौ सूर्यः","that sun"],["उद्यन्न् उद्गच्छन्","rising, coming up"],["अस्तम् अदर्शनम्","setting, becoming unseen"],["यन् गच्छन्","as it moves"],["क्षणो नीतः","the moment that has passed"],["तस्य आयुः ऋते वर्जयित्वा","apart from that, the life [remaining]"],["वृथैव हरति","it takes it away in vain"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":18,"end":18,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["ननु जीवनम् एव","surely life itself"],["आयुषः फलम् अस्ति","is the fruit of one's lifespan"],["भस्त्राः चर्म-कोशाः","bellows are leather bags"],["न खादन्ति न अश्नन्ति","they do not eat"],["न मेहन्ति","they do not emit semen"],["रे