hands are like that"],["लसती काञ्चन-कङ्कणे ययोः","on which golden bracelets shine"],["अपि-अर्थे वा-शब्दः","the particle vā has the sense of api"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":22,"end":22,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["विष्णोर् मूर्तीर् न निरीक्षेते","if the eyes do not behold the forms of Viṣṇu"],["ते बर्हायिते","those eyes are like peacock feathers"],["मयूर-पिञ्छ-तुल्ये नेत्रे","eyes resembling peacock plumes"],["द्रुमवत् जन्म भजेते","the two are like trees by their birth"],["वृक्ष-मूल-तुल्यौ","like the roots of trees"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":23,"end":23,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["नाभिलभेत","one should not touch or grasp"],["अभितो न स्पृशेत् न धारयेत्","one should neither touch nor hold"],["श्री-विष्णु-पद्याः","of the feet of Śrī Viṣṇu"],["श्री-विष्णु-पद-लग्नायाः","attached to the feet of Lord Viṣṇu"],["न वेदेति","‘does not smell’"],["अवघ्राय न अभिनन्देत्","having smelled, he should not express delight"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":24,"end":24,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["अश्मवत् सारः","firm like stone"],["बलं काठिन्यम्","strength means hardness"],["विक्रिया-लक्षणम् आह","he explains the characteristic of transformation"],["गात्र-रुहेषु रोमसु","in the hairs growing on the body"],["हर्षः उद्गमः","horripilation is their rising"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":3,"start":25,"end":25,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/03_devopAsanam.md","source_blob_sha":"f1c36df7573988b5b723cbb9aac6ff2359092bb8","pairs":[["अभक्तस्य","for a non-devotee"],["सर्वम् एतद् व्यर्थम्","all of this is useless"],["मनसः अनुकूलं प्रियम् च","dear and pleasing to the mind"],["ब्रूषे","you have spoken"],["अतः साधु पृष्टः सन्","therefore, having been properly asked"],["वैयासकिः नृपतिं प्रति","Śuka, son of Vyāsa, to the king"],["यद् आह तद् अभिधेहि","tell me what he said"]]}]}